WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Have you ever wondered
if there’s a natural way

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.160
to lower your high blood pressure,
guard against Alzheimer's,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.440
lose weight, and feel better?
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.680
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.840
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.720
It may come as no
surprise that what we eat

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.760
directly affects our chances
of getting skin cancer.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.720
In our first story, we look
at the best supplement

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.120
for preventing skin cancer.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.920
Nicotinamide,
also known as niacinamide,

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.760
is a form of vitamin B3

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.600
that has been used topically
for decades

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.256
in the cosmetic field
to prevent skin aging.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.120
So, researchers decided
to put it to the test orally

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.320
for skin cancer prevention.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.240
In a petri dish,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.160
skin samples taken
from breast reduction

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.400
and tummy tuck surgeries

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.360
exposed to UV
with or without niacinamide

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.880
found that it enhanced
DNA repair.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.440
Would this translate out
into less cancer?

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.720
In a Phase II trial,
dozens of individuals

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.600
with four or more
precancerous actinic keratoses

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.520
each were randomized
to take a placebo

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.120
or 500 mg of niacinamide
once or twice a day.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.920
Within two months,
there was a 35 percent reduction

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.520
in actinic keratoses
in the twice-a-day group,

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:14.800
and a 15 percent reduction

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.400
in the once-a-day group
compared to placebo.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.440
It's not that they developed
fewer in those months,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.800
but more
spontaneously disappeared

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.800
in the niacinamide groups.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.320
What about actual cancers?

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.320
By month four, there were
five times fewer cancers

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.480
(11 placebo participants
developed 20 new skin cancers

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.480
versus only two
niacinamide participants

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.160
developing a total
of four new cancers).

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.160
Normally, it would be difficult
to fund studies

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.040
on nonpatentable products that
only cost a few cents a day,

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.400
but the results of this
and a similar study

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.960
on organ transplant patients

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.720
were so extraordinary
ONTRAC was born.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.920
Oral Nicotinamide
to Reduce Actinic Cancer

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.440
was a publicly-funded
phase III trial

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.960
randomizing hundreds of people

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.040
with a personal history
of skin cancers

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.400
(actinic means UV-induced)

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.320
to 500 mg of nicotinamide
twice daily

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.920
or placebo for a full year.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.920
By the end, there were
25 percent fewer cancers

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.600
with no significant
side effects

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.800
for just pennies a day.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.200
You have to keep it up, though.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.960
At a six-month follow-up
after the study was over,

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.280
the cancer rates equalized back
to baseline rates.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.240
What are the downsides?

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.560
A study of 500 people

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.320
put on up to three grams
of niacinamide a day

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.720
for five years (trying
to prevent type 1 diabetes)

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.040
unearthed no adverse effects
over placebo

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.040
(though it failed to prevent
type 1 diabetes).

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.920
The high tolerance
of niacinamide

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.480
is partly due
to its water-soluble nature,

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.320
such that you just pee out
any excess.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:50.360
But those with end-stage
kidney failure on dialysis

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.020
don't have functioning kidneys,

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.520
and so, blood levels
should be monitored,

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.800
as, in that context,
niacinamide can cause

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.560
a serious, though reversible,
drop in platelets,

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.040
which are important
for blood clotting.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.920
High enough doses may become
toxic to the liver, though,

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.160
even with normal kidneys.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.040
Vasodilatory side effects,
like facial flushing,

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.800
attributed to niacinamide
in some older studies

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.640
were likely due
to a less purified form

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.120
contaminated with
residual niacin.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.400
(I know it's confusing!

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.680
Niacin, also known
as nicotinic acid,

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.440
is the precursor of,
but very different from,

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.200
niacinamide, which is
synonymous with nicotinamide.)

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.360
One concern
regarding any treatment

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.360
for a largely lifestyle disease

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.400
is that individuals may neglect
other defensive measures,

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.520
overconfident in
the supplement's protection.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.360
Regarding drug interactions,
a concern has been raised

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.160
about taking niacinamide
together with carbamazepine,

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.920
a popular anti-seizure drug
(sold as Tegretol).

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.000
But, in general,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.000
as the ONTRAC researchers
concluded,

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.040
"Oral nicotinamide
is safe and effective

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.200
in reducing the rates
of new nonmelanoma skin cancers

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.120
and precancerous growths
in high-risk patients."

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.000
To their credit, a 2021 survey
of skin cancer surgeons found

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.400
that three-quarters
recommended its use.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.040
Other than nicotinamide,
how else might we protect

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.760
against skin cancer
from the inside out?

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.479
That's what I'll cover next.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.360
Millions of skin cancers
are diagnosed every year,

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.680
the most common cancer
in the United States.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.280
I've covered the single
most important thing we can do-

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.988
protect against exposure
to UV radiation.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.000
What about dietary protection?

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.800
The first study to elucidate
the effect of diet

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.680
on UV-induced tumors
found that high-fat diets

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.200
accelerated tumor formation
in mice.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.120
Within six months of UV,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.120
fifty percent of the high-fat
fed mice had tumors

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.480
compared to only 16
in the control-fed group.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.080
Encouragingly,
switching the mice

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.840
to a low-fat diet
after the exposure

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:56.240
was able to negate the tumor
exacerbating high-fat effects.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.520
In people, a dietary pattern

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.200
characterized by meat
and fat consumption

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:03.000
was associated
with up to a near quadrupling

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.800
of squamous cell
carcinoma risk,

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.960
the second most common type
of skin cancer,

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.600
whereas a vegetable
and fruit pattern

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.040
was associated
with a halving of risk

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.760
(apparently driven largely
by the intake of greens).

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.480
All we needed now
was to randomize people

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.160
to low-fat diets
and see if cancer

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.320
could be prevented
in people too,

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.440
and, thanks to National
Cancer Institute funding

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.360
and a Veteran Affairs
research team,

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.320
the striking results
were published

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.640
in the New England
Journal of Medicine.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.880
Seventy-six patients
with a history of skin cancer

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.240
(and, therefore, at high risk
of developing more)

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:38.080
were randomized to continue
to eat their regular diets

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:41.040
or switch to a quote-unquote
"low-fat" diet

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.560
of 20 percent of calories
from fat.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.160
I put low-fat in quotes

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.520
because that's actually
a high-fat diet

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:51.600
compared to what's normal
for our species.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.000
For millions of years,
our ancestors may have evolved

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.600
getting approximately
10 percent

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.280
of our calories from fat.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:58.640
For millions of years,

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.960
about 99.8 percent
of our time on Earth,

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.960
it was virtually impossible
for us to consume regularly

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.440
more than 10 to 15 percent
of calories as fat.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:11.720
So, that's a normal fat diet
for the human species.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:14.840
A low-fat diet
would be less than that.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:18.480
Though 20 percent is certainly
comparatively low fat

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.040
compared to the current
adult average

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.600
in the United States
of 37 percent.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.800
Would a drop down to 20
make a difference?

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.440
Researchers tracked
the appearance

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.160
of actinic keratoses,
rough scaly patches

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:34.440
that are premalignant lesions
that turn into skin cancer,

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.440
over the next two years.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.560
The average patient
in the control group

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.600
developed 10 lesions
in those two years,

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.040
compared to just three
in the lower-fat group.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.080
Okay, but what about
actual skin cancers?

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.840
The results were so exciting

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.800
the same team of researchers
randomized

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.200
hundreds
of skin cancer patients

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.880
to the same two diets.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.160
By the end of the study,

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:58.560
the skin cancer rate
was 10 times lower

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.960
in the lower-fat group.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.680
Now this is no clarion call
for SnackWell's cookies.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:06.000
Although fat appears
twice as bad,

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.600
high-refined carb consumption
was also found to be

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.080
significantly associated
with skin wrinkling and atrophy

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.880
among a nationwide
cross-section

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.320
of middle-aged women.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.640
Those who consistently have

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.800
higher than normal
fasting blood sugars

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.600
are perceived to be
nearly a half year older

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:21.560
than they really are

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:25.160
for every 18 points higher
their average blood sugars are.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:28.000
So, those with a prediabetic
fasting blood sugar

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.000
of like 120 milligrams
per deciliter

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.000
look about a year older
than those regularly having

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.200
a normal fasting blood sugar
of around 75.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.280
Now, the Women's Health
Initiative randomized

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.400
nearly 50,000
postmenopausal women

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.520
to a recommendation
to eat the same lower-fat diet;

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.000
yet, there was no change

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.840
in the incidence
of skin cancer.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:49.800
This is not surprising
given the poor adherence.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.000
Only 31 percent of the women
in the intervention group

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.680
complied with
the dietary recommendations.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.120
It turns out healthy diets
may only work

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.760
if you actually eat them.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:04.120
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:07.800
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.520
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:14.280
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:19.160
If you want to see any graphs, charts,
graphics, images, or studies mentioned here,

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.400
please go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.480
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:28.200
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:31.360
My latest book, “How Not to Age”
is out now.

